## Key design decisions

- CON-2: aws-amplify v6 generateClient, Lambda authMode, ID token from Pool B SRP
- CON-3: output:'export', all data fetching client-side after auth
- CON-5: tenantId from ID-token claim in useTenantSubscription, never in mutation inputs
- CON-6: role gating presentation-only via canApprove(role, module), server enforces
- CON-8: CARD-7 justification required before approve mutation fires on flagged items
- B1: Observable .subscribe(), not for-await (Amplify v6 contract)
- B2: LocaleProvider static-imports all 3 catalogs, keys on user.locale
- B3: fetchAuthSession() per call auto-refreshes expired tokens
- R1: Edit & approve parses args from draftBody, sends object as editedPayload
- R2: Approved items exempt from subscription/poll removal, 10s + dismiss
- M5: images:{unoptimized:true} for static export compatibility
- m5: Unit test asserts globals.css and cssVariables export match
